# -*- text -*-
##
## modules/pam -- PAM authentication module (rlm_pam)
##
## Hands authentication off to Linux PAM. Requires:
##   - rlm_pam.so present in the FreeRADIUS image (upstream
##     `freeradius/freeradius-server` ships it on the standard variant).
##   - A PAM service config at `/etc/pam.d/<pam_auth>` inside the container
##     (the upstream image ships `/etc/pam.d/radiusd` by default). To use a
##     custom service name, override `modules.pam.pam_auth` AND mount
##     a PAM config file via `extraVolumes` / `extraVolumeMounts`.
##   - Virtual server wiring: set `Auth-Type := PAM` in the `authorize`
##     section, and add `pam` to the `authenticate {}` block.
##
## NOTE: rendered through Helm `tpl` (see templates/configmap/modules.yaml).
## Every key under `modules.pam` in values.yaml (except `enabled`) is rendered
## into the block below via `freeradius.tplvalues.renderConfig`, which emits
## FreeRADIUS-style `key = value` directives (so `pam_auth: radiusd` becomes
## `pam_auth = radiusd`; a `Pam-Auth` attribute set in `authorize` overrides it).
##
pam {
{{- with omit .Values.modules.pam "enabled" }}
{{- include "freeradius.tplvalues.renderConfig" (dict "value" . "context" $) | nindent 4 }}
{{- end }}
}
